Seq,\\\"write_id\\\":\\\"write-new\\\"})\n   nodes[1].ReadIndex([]byte(requestCtx));pump()\n   barrierSeq:=0\n   if len(readStates[1])==1 {\n    rs:=readStates[1][0]\n    barrierSeq=emit(\\\"read_barrier_received\\\",map[string]interface{}{\\\"read_admission_seq\\\":readSeq,\\\"read_index\\\":rs.Index,\\\"request_ctx\\\":string(rs.RequestCtx)})\n   } else {emit(\\\"no_immediate_barrier\\\",nil)}''')\ns=s.replace('emit(\\\"read_consumption\\\",map[string]interface{}{\\\"read_index\\\":rs.Index,\\\"request_ctx\\\":string(rs.RequestCtx),\\\"strict_application_boundary\\\":applied[1]>rs.Index,\\\"observed_value\\\":values[1]})','''if applied[1]>rs.Index {\n     serveSeq:=emit(\\\"ready_to_serve\\\",map[string]interface{}{\\\"barrier_seq\\\":barrierSeq,\\\"read_index\\\":rs.Index,\\\"request_ctx\\\":string(rs.RequestCtx),\\\"strict_application_boundary\\\":applied[1]>rs.Index})\n     emit(\\\"read_completed\\\",map[string]interface{}{\\\"serve_seq\\\":serveSeq,\\\"read_index\\\":rs.Index,\\\"request_ctx\\\":string(rs.RequestCtx),\\\"observed_value\\\":values[1]})\n    } else {emit(\\\"application_boundary_missing\\\",map[string]interface{}{\\\"read_index\\\":rs.Index})}''')\nPath('demoted_read_check_test.go').write_text(s)\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));q=next(c['question'] for c in r['candidates'] if c.get('id')=='5209d9e49f24439d8efc2884c5d1630e');q['disposition']='ready_for_check';q['unknowns']=[];q['source_ids']+=['S-demotion','S-ready-softstate'];q['trigger_rationale']='Exploration ffa48fdd7b904ab3b91aa6c0db02b712 reached a complete stale read: new singleton voter applied write new at index 7 before ReadIndex on the demoted learner; the old leader returned barrier 5, later applied actual prefix through 6, and the caller satisfying applied>5 observed old. Public Ready says SoftState need not be consumed and imposes no invalidation of a returned matching-context ReadState on a later term change. This justifies a fixed fresh check comparing the completed read value to its causally preceding write.'\nclaim=dict(id='C-demoted-read-linearizability',kind='obligation',concern='consensus_safety',description='With ReadOnlySafe, a caller using a fresh request context and a matching returned ReadState, and waiting until local application is strictly beyond its index, must not complete a read that omits a write completed before that read invocation when there is no intervening overwriting write. This remains required when a voter is legally demoted to a learner with StepDownOnRemoval disabled.',source_ids=['S-read-safe-contract','S-read-contract','S-ready-read-contract','S-stepdown-option'],scope=dict(description='Linearizable single-register read from a retained learner after legal joint demotion of its prior leader, with StepDownOnRemoval=false. A new singleton voter has completed a write before read admission; network delays can make the learner unaware of the new term until after the local ReadState is returned.',assumptions=['Fresh unique ReadIndex context and matching returned context.','Caller applies entries in log order, processes Ready persistence before messages, and consumes the read only with applied>ReadState.Index.','One completed register write and no later overwriting write.','CFT network may delay/drop genuine messages without forging, editing or dropping local completion responses.'],excluded=['Caller serving before the documented application boundary.','ReadOnlyLeaseBased and custom clock/lease assumptions.','StepDownOnRemoval=true as a formal scenario; it is a diagnostic control.']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=['S-proposal','S-singleton','S-config','S-demotion','S-ready','S-read','S-read-entry'],expectation_ids=['S-read-safe-contract','S-read-contract','S-ready-read-contract','S-stepdown-option','S-ready-softstate'],binding_ids=['L-singleton-read','L-demotion-role','L-read-response'],derivation='ReadOnlySafe promises linearizability; Node.ReadIndex/Ready specify a returned matching-context barrier and the local application threshold. A completed read after a completed write must include that write if no later write changes it. The construction honors the stricter literal applied>index wording. The demoted replica remains a learner, not a stopped removed member. StepDownOnRemoval is optional and its false setting has no documented reduction of ReadOnlySafe. Ready says SoftState need not be consumed, so adding caller-side term invalidation would introduce an extra duty absent from the supplied API.',applicability='The learner receives its barrier locally before learning the higher term, then finishes application of a real prefix beyond the barrier while the newer completed write is still undelivered.',alternatives=['StepDownOnRemoval=true prevents this source path in the diagnostic control.','Greater applied index alone does not fix a barrier already below a write completed before the read invocation.']))\nbindings=[]\nfor id,mat,sym,a,b,desc in [('L-singleton-read','S-proposal','stepLeader',1346,1373,'Singleton read shortcut returns local commit without verifying the local node is the singleton voter.'),('L-demotion-role','S-config','switchToConfig',1975,2004,'Demotion leaves leader role intact when optional stepdown is disabled.'),('L-read-response','S-read','responseToReadIndexReq',2070,2086,'Local read returns a ReadState index and original request context.')]:\n bindings.append(dict(id=id,material_id=mat,symbol=sym,start_line=a,end_line=b,description=desc,pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim['id'],source_ids=['S-read-safe-contract','S-ready-read-contract',mat],rationale='This path generates or qualifies the barrier on which the documented local read completion relies.')]))\nfeedback=dict(ref_ids=['ffa48fdd7b904ab3b91aa6c0db02b712','5209d9e49f24439d8efc2884c5d1630e','B-read','F-config','S-demotion','S-ready-read-contract','S-read-safe-contract'],answered='The exploration completed legal demotion to learner, retained StateLeader with StepDownOnRemoval=false, elected remaining voter 2 in term 3 and applied new at index 7 before the read. Node 1 returned ReadState index 5, later applied the new leader no-op through index 6, and the caller satisfying the strict application rule observed old. Stepdown-enabled control returned no ReadState. This remains construction knowledge, not formal Evidence.',remaining=['Fresh fixed execution and correspondence review of read identity, actual message prefix and completed state-machine observations.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Actual read completion closes the earlier consumer gap; the result is not inferred merely from a low returned index. Sources give no extra caller obligation to discard a returned local ReadState on a later SoftState change.')\ncandidate=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id='5209d9e49f24439d8efc2884c5d1630e',question=q,obligation=claim,bindings=bindings,rationale='Ground the ReadOnlySafe responsibility using the public API and the reached strict-boundary history.')\nB=[x['id'] for x in bindings]\ndef eq(f,v):return dict(field=f,op='eq',value=v)\ndef ref(f,x):return dict(field=f,op='eq',reference=x)\nsrc=['S-read-safe-contract','S-read-contract','S-ready-read-contract','S-ready-softstate','S-stepdown-option','S-demotion','S-proposal','S-singleton','S-config','S-read','S-read-entry','S-ready','S-advance','S-bootstrap','S-log','S-response','S-roles','S-step','S-storage-append','S-heartbeat-producer']\nplan=dict(description='Generate a complete write-before-read history on two real RawNodes. Implicit joint demotion changes voters {1,2} to voter {2}, learner {1}. After finalization isolate old leader 1, campaign node 2 and complete register write new. Invoke ReadIndex on node 1 with fresh context, retain actual Ready.ReadStates, then deliver only generated entry data through the preceding no-op index. Serve the read only after strict applied>read index and compare its real register value to the preceding completed write.',claim_id=claim['id'],binding_ids=B,harness=dict(kind='go_test',source='',files={},description='Single-goroutine deterministic register application and real RawNode/MemoryStorage processing. Each application is consecutive and updates the register only for nonempty normal entries. Sender messages are generated by target code, queued FIFO, then selected for delivery/drop by declared phase and entry index. Appends with a higher commit hint but only the allowed prefix are delivered unchanged; follower maybeAppend bounds commitment. The stepdown=true scenario is a diagnostic control.',semantic_changes=['Simulated unreliable transport: normal delivery for all configuration work, full isolation during new election/write/read-barrier acquisition, then drop entries above the selected actual no-op prefix and heartbeats whose commit exceeds that prefix. No message bytes or target state are altered.','In-memory stable storage models successful persistence, without crashes.','Application is a deterministic one-register state machine; all reads and mutations occur on the same goroutine.'],prerequisites=[dict(alias='written',event='write_completed',conditions=[eq('stepdown',False),eq('write_id','write-new'),eq('write_applied',True),eq('write_value','new')]),dict(alias='admit',event='read_admitted',conditions=[eq('stepdown',False),ref('write_completion_seq','written.history_seq'),eq('old_is_learner',True),eq('old_role','StateLeader')]),dict(alias='barrier',event='read_barrier_received',conditions=[eq('stepdown',False),ref('read_admission_seq','admit.history_seq')]),dict(alias='serve',event='ready_to_serve',conditions=[eq('stepdown',False),ref('barrier_seq','barrier.history_seq'),ref('read_index','barrier.read_index'),eq('strict_application_boundary',True)])],legality=dict(source_ids=src,expectation_ids=['S-read-contract','S-ready-read-contract','S-ready-softstate','S-stepdown-option'],binding_ids=B,derivation='Public Bootstrap/Campaign/ProposeConfChange create the prefix; implicit joint demotion and exit complete before isolation. Caller persists and applies every Ready before Advance and checks consecutive application. The only write operation is new; its completion is measured at actual committed/applied index before ReadIndex invocation. ReadState is copied out of Ready by context and retained by the caller; no API requires SoftState consumption or later-term invalidation. Network phases use actual outputs only and may drop data beyond the selected prefix, which is the actual applied index of the newly elected singleton leader before the write. Dropping data while delivering independently generated heartbeat messages is ordinary unreliable network behavior; no local ordering/persistence duty is relaxed.',applicability='ReadOnlySafe, default disabled stepdown formal input, retained learner participation and strict application threshold. Pending/no-barrier control produces diagnostics only.',unresolved=[])),monitors=[dict(id='M-demoted-read',checker_id='P-demoted-read',event='read_completed',binding_ids=B,admission_alias='admit',applicability_conditions=[eq('stepdown',False)],grounding=dict(source_ids=src,expectation_ids=['S-read-safe-contract','S-read-contract','S-ready-read-contract'],binding_ids=B,derivation='The stable operation and request_ctx identity correlate the actual write completion, later read admission, target-produced barrier and strict application witness. Read result is the caller register value after serving conditions; assertion compares it to written.write_value. Sequence references declare causal predecessors without using a value as identity. There is one write and no overwrite, so a different completed read value contradicts the scoped linearizability requirement. Missing read/barrier/application/result stays unknown, never false or holds.',applicability='Independent stepdown=false input; stepdown=true outputs excluded before prerequisite requirements.'))],observable_properties=[dict(checker_id='P-demoted-read',kind='event_assertion',trigger=eq('stepd